re><div class="collection-copy"><p class="featured-label">Featured story</p><p class="eyebrow">SHIVA / COMPASSION</p><h3>Shiva drinks Halahala</h3><p>When the ocean yields a terrible poison, Shiva acts to protect the worlds.</p><p class="story-card-meta"><span>Full story</span><span>{{ storyCatalog.halahala.minutes }} min read</span></p><a class="tale-card-link" href="{{ storyCatalog.halahala.href }}">Read the story <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a><p class="collection-source">Source: <a href="/sources.html#ref-shiva-poison">Bhagavata Purana, Skandha 8, Chapter 7</a></p></div></article><article class="collection-card" data-deity="Rama" data-format="full" data-scripture="Ramayana" data-theme="Dharma" id="story-rama-exile"><figure><img alt="Rama, Sita and Lakshmana leaving Ayodhya for the forest" loading="lazy" src="/assets/images/rama-exile.webp"/><figcaption>AI-GENERATED ILLUSTRATION</figcaption></figure><div class="collection-copy"><p class="eyebrow">RAMA / DHARMA</p><h3>Rama leaves Ayodhya</h3><p>A royal coronation gives way to exile, and a family must face the meaning of duty.</p><p class="story-card-meta"><span>Full story</span><span>{{ storyCatalog.rama.minutes }} min read</span></p><a class="tale-card-link" href="{{ storyCatalog.rama.href }}">Read the story <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a><p class="collection-source">Source: <a href="/sources.html#ref-rama-exile">Ramayana, Ayodhya Kanda</a></p></div></article><article class="collection-card" data-deity="Hanuman" data-format="full" data-scripture="Ramayana" data-theme="Courage" id="story-hanuman-lanka"><figure><img alt="Hanuman crossing the ocean toward Lanka in search of Sita" height="1024" loading="lazy" src="/assets/images/hanuman-lanka.webp" width="1536"/><figcaption>AI-GENERATED ILLUSTRATION</figcaption></figure><div class="collection-copy"><p class="eyebrow">HANUMAN / COURAGE</p><h3>Hanuman’s leap to Lanka</h3><p>Across the ocean lies the next step in the search for Sita.</p><p class="story-card-meta"><span>Full story</span><span>{{ storyCatalog.hanuman.minutes }} min read</span></p><a class="tale-card-link" href="{{ storyCatalog.hanuman.href }}">Read the story <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a><p class="collection-source">Source: <a href="/sources.html#ref-hanuman-lanka">Ramayana, Sundara Kanda</a></p></div></article><article class="collection-card" data-deity="Krishna" data-scripture="Bhagavata Purana" data-theme="Protection" id="story-govardhana"><figure><img alt="Krishna lifting Govardhana to shelter villagers and cattle from the rain" loading="lazy" src="/assets/images/govardhana.webp"/><figcaption>AI-GENERATED ILLUSTRATION</figcaption></figure><div class="collection-copy"><p class="eyebrow">KRISHNA / PROTECTION</p><h3>Krishna lifts Govardhana</h3><p>A mountain becomes a shelter for the people and cattle of Vraja.</p><p class="story-card-meta"><span>Full story</span><span>{{ storyCatalog.govardhana.minutes }} min read</span></p><a class="tale-card-link" href="{{ storyCatalog.govardhana.href }}">Read the story <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a><p class="collection-source">Source: <a href="/sources.html#ref-govardhana">Bhagavata Purana, Skandha 10, chapters 24–27</a></p></div></article><article class="collection-card" data-deity="Devi" data-format="full" data-scripture="Markandeya Purana" data-theme="Courage" id="story-mahishasura"><figure><img alt="Durga riding her lion before Mahishasura in buffalo form" loading="lazy" src="/assets/images/durga-mahishasura.webp"/><figcaption>AI-GENERATED ILLUSTRATION</figcaption></figure><div class="collection-copy"><p class="eyebrow">DEVI / COURAGE</p><h3>Devi and Mahishasura</h3><p>The gods’ combined radiance takes divine form in the struggle against Mahishasura.</p><p class="story-card-meta"><span>Full story</span><span>{{ storyCatalog.mahishasura.minutes }} min read</span></p><a class="tale-card-link" href="{{ storyCatalog.mahishasura.href }}">Read the story <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a><p class="collection-source">Source: <a href="/sources.html#ref-mahishasura">Markandeya Purana, Devi Mahatmya</a></p></div></article><article class="collection-card" data-deity="Devi" data-format="full" data-scripture="Brahmanda Purana" data-theme="Protection" id="story-lalita-bhandasura"><figure><img alt="Lalita holding noose, goad, sugarcane bow and flower arrows amid sunrise radiance" loading="lazy" src="/assets/images/lalita-manifestation.webp"/><figcaption>AI-GENERATED DEVOTIONAL ILLUSTRATION</figcaption></figure><div class="collection-copy"><p class="eyebrow">DEVI / PROTECTION</p><h3>Lalita and Bhandasura</h3><p>Enter the sacred narrative of Lalita Tripurasundari and her divine army.</p><p class="story-card-meta"><span>Full story</span><span>{{ storyCatalog.lalita.minutes }} min read</span></p><a class="tale-card-link" href="{{ storyCatalog.lalita.href }}">Read the story <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a><p class="collection-source">Source: <a href="/sources.html#ref-lalita-bhandasura">Brahmanda Purana, Lalita Mahatmya</a></p></div></article><article class="collection-card" data-format="full" data-deity="Sages &amp; devotees" data-scripture="Ramayana" data-theme="Devotion" id="story-bhagiratha-ganga"><figure><img alt="Bhagiratha in devotion as Ganga descends into Shiva’s matted hair" height="1024" loading="lazy" src="/assets/images/bhagiratha-ganga.webp" width="1536"/><figcaption>AI-GENERATED ILLUSTRATION</figcaption></figure><div class="collection-copy"><p class="eyebrow">SAGES &amp; DEVOTEES / DEVOTION</p><h3>Bhagiratha brings the Ganga</h3><p>A king’s perseverance brings a heavenly river to the earth.</p><p class="story-card-meta"><span>Full story</span><span>{{ storyCatalog.bhagiratha.minutes }} min read</span></p><a class="tale-card-link" href="{{ storyCatalog.bhagiratha.href }}">Read the story <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a><p class="collection-source">Source: <a href="/sources.html#ref-bhagiratha-ganga">Ramayana, Bala Kanda</a></p></div></article><article class="collection-card" data-deity="Shiva" data-format="full" data-scripture="Shiva Purana" data-theme="Devotion" id="story-shiva-parvati"><figure><img alt="Shiva and Parvati exchanging garlands at their Himalayan wedding" loading="lazy" src="/assets/images/shiva-parvati-card.webp"/><figcaption>AI-GENERATED ILLUSTRATION</figcaption></figure><div class="collection-copy"><p class="eyebrow">SHIVA &amp; PARVATI / DEVOTION</p><h3>Shiva and Parvati</h3><p>From Parvati’s tapas to the divine wedding: a story of devotion, resolve and recognition.</p><p class="story-card-meta"><span>Full story</span><span>{{ storyCatalog.parvati.minutes }} min read</span></p><a class="tale-card-link" href="{{ storyCatalog.parvati.href }}">Read the story <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a><p class="collection-source">Source: <a href="/sources.html#ref-shiva-parvati">Shiva Purana, Parvati Khanda</a></p></div></article><article class="collection-card" data-deity="Sages &amp; devotees" data-format="full" data-scripture="Bhagavata Purana" data-theme="Devotion" id="story-dhruva"><figure><img src="/assets/images/dhruva-card.webp" alt="Young Dhruva leaving an imagined palace for a forest path" width="1536" height="1024" loading="lazy"><figcaption>AI-GENERATED NARRATIVE INTERPRETATION</figcaption></figure><div class="collection-copy"><p class="eyebrow">DHRUVA / DEVOTION</p><h3>Dhruva’s search for the Divine</h3><p>A child leaves the palace seeking honour, and discovers a greater object of devotion.</p><p class="story-card-meta"><span>Full story</span><span>{{ storyCatalog.dhruva.minutes }} min read</span></p><a class="tale-card-link" href="{{ storyCatalog.dhruva.href }}">Read the story <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a><p class="collection-source">Source: <a href="/sources.html#ref-dhruva">Bhagavata Purana, Skandha 4, chapters 8–9</a></p></div></article></div><div class="collection-empty" hidden="" id="no-stories"><h3>A different doorway awaits.</h3><p>No stories match this combination. Try another